1 0 0 1 50 665 Tm
(following Lindeman’s 10% Law across trophic levels \(Producers -> Primary) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 650 Tm
(Consumers -> Secondary -> Tertiary\).) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 628 Tm
(Ecological Pyramids: Pyramid of Energy is ALWAYS upright because energy is) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 613 Tm
(lost as metabolic heat at every step. Pyramid of Biomass is upright in) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 598 Tm
(terrestrial ecosystems but inverted in aquatic ecosystems \(standing crop of) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 583 Tm
(phytoplankton is smaller than zooplankton\). Pyramid of Numbers can be) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 568 Tm
(inverted in tree ecosystems supporting numerous parasites.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 546 Tm
(Ecotone is a transition zone between two distinct biomes \(e.g., mangrove) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 531 Tm
(between marine and terrestrial\), exhibiting high species richness known as) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 516 Tm
(the Edge Effect.) Tj
